name issue_152_alr_request_probe_v2
describe probe_v2_cross_traffic on seed 4: with libwebrtc's ALR settings (80/40/-60) the sender is in ALR when the competing flow joins, so the probe after the drop (ProbeController::RequestProbe) goes out (#152)
# libwebrtc's AlrDetector runs with WebRTC-ProbingScreenshareBwe's default "1.0,2875,80,40,-60,3"
# (alr_experiment.cc), read from its live budget in sm_compare (PR #210): in ALR from 5.7 to 13.6 s on
# probe_v2_cross_traffic seed 1, and it probes 0.85 x the pre-drop rate at 12.3 s. With 0.65/0.80/0.50 our
# detector was never in ALR, so RequestProbe never probed. On seed 4 the probe now goes out:
# target 2008 -> 2081 kbps, utilization 65.7 -> 68.4 %. probe_v2_cross_traffic over seeds 1-10 (libwebrtc
# from parity-data): queue p95 mean 221.5 -> 230.1 ms (libwebrtc 251.2), target 2172 -> 2240 kbps (2257).
seed 4
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=3000kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=1500kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
# PR #401 (#399, RTCP schedule drawn per seed on both stacks; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was >= 2040. Ours 2033 on seed 4
# (seeds 4-13 2033-2373). Seed-4 outlier; mean in band (ours 2179 / libwebrtc 2193; libwebrtc per-seed not published); 5 % below ours.
expect cc.target_avg_kbps >= 1930
# #390 (needs-human): with the cross traffic ahead of the call's packets in a shared millisecond, as in sm_compare,
# this seed reads 67.4 (was 68.4). Signed off by the Owner on #395: seed-4 outlier; mean in band (ours 71.2 / libwebrtc 71.9),
# seeds 4-13.
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 64
expect video.freeze_count == 0
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 250
expect cc.unsettled == 0
